  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. PASSING: At the start of each hand, players select three cards from their hand and pass them face-down to another player (Left, Right, Across, or Hold in rotation).\n2. THE LEAD: The player holding the 2 of Clubs leads the first trick.\n3. TRICK RULES: Players must follow suit if possible. If they cannot follow suit, they may play any card, including a penalty card (except on the very first trick).\n4. WINNING TRICKS: The highest card of the suit led wins the trick and leads the next.\n5. LIMITS: Hearts cannot be led until a Heart has been 'broken' (discarded on a previous trick).",
    Player: "1. PASSING: At the start of each hand, players select three cards from their hand and pass them face-down to another player (Left, Right, Across, or Hold in rotation).\n2. THE LEAD: The player holding the 2 of Clubs leads the first trick.\n3. TRICK RULES: Players must follow suit if possible. If they cannot follow suit, they may play any card, including a penalty card (except on the very first trick).\n4. WINNING TRICKS: The highest card of the suit led wins the trick and leads the next.\n5. LIMITS: Hearts cannot be led until a Heart has been 'broken' (discarded on a previous trick).",
    objective: 'Have the lowest score at the end of the game by avoiding taking tricks containing Hearts or the Queen of Spades.',
    gameplay: "1. PASSING: At the start of each hand, players select three cards from their hand and pass them face-down to another player (Left, Right, Across, or Hold in rotation).\n2. THE LEAD: The player holding the 2 of Clubs leads the first trick.\n3. TRICK RULES: Players must follow suit if possible. If they cannot follow suit, they may play any card, including a penalty card (except on the very first trick).\n4. WINNING TRICKS: The highest card of the suit led wins the trick and leads the next.\n5. LIMITS: Hearts cannot be led until a Heart has been 'broken' (discarded on a previous trick).",
    keyRules: [
      'Must follow suit if possible.',
      'Penalty cards: Each Heart (1 point), Queen of Spades (13 points).',
      'Shooting the Moon: If a player takes ALL penalty cards (all 13 Hearts and the Queen of Spades), they score 0, and everyone else scores 26.',
      'Hearts cannot be led unless they have been broken or the leader has only Hearts left.',
